1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,875
bobliu O S: a from scratch thirty two bit x86 operating system.

2
00:00:04,875 --> 00:00:08,356
It boots, forks, pipes, runs Lua, and plays DOOM.

3
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:14,232
bobliu is a hobby kernel written to learn how every layer fits together.

4
00:00:14,232 --> 00:00:20,390
Its own bootstrap, interrupts, paging, allocators, scheduler, file systems, libc, shell and

5
00:00:20,390 --> 00:00:21,405
core utilities.

6
00:00:21,405 --> 00:00:24,044
No Linux, no borrowed kernel, no glibc.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,907
User programs run in ring three on top of the libc.

8
00:00:27,907 --> 00:00:32,797
They enter the kernel through int eighty with Linux i three eighty six syscall numbers.

9
00:00:32,797 --> 00:00:37,800
The kernel has a process layer with a preemptive scheduler and copy on write fork, a file

10
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:41,004
system layer behind a V F S, a memory layer, and drivers.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,834
That adds up to 21,526 lines of C and assembly: 7,313 in the kernel, 9,478 in the libc, which

12
00:00:50,834 --> 00:00:56,628
includes a vendored math library, and 4,735 in user programs.

13
00:00:57,630 --> 00:01:01,756
A fresh clone builds a bootable I S O of 51.6 megabytes.

14
00:01:01,756 --> 00:01:04,334
The kernel itself is 453 kilobytes.

15
00:01:04,334 --> 00:01:08,312
Most of the initial ramdisk is the Freedoom game data.

16
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:15,075
What ships: a kernel with copy on write fork, a preemptive scheduler, threads, signals, pipes

17
00:01:15,075 --> 00:01:16,563
and its own file system.

18
00:01:16,563 --> 00:01:20,841
A userland of 80 programs, with a shell, vi, the kilo editor and Lua.

19
00:01:20,841 --> 00:01:25,800
And two big ports: Doom, and the real Neovim, which is slow to start under QEMU.

20
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:31,354
Pipes work, Lua runs, and the finale is Doom, launched from the shell.

21
00:01:32,350 --> 00:01:33,049
The limits.

22
00:01:33,049 --> 00:01:35,525
Single core, at most sixteen processes.

23
00:01:35,525 --> 00:01:38,701
The bobfs file system has no cache and no journal.

24
00:01:38,701 --> 00:01:41,241
Kernel mode exceptions halt the machine.

25
00:01:41,241 --> 00:01:43,718
There is no networking, sound or U S B.

26
00:01:43,718 --> 00:01:46,639
It is a learning O S, not a Linux replacement.

27
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:53,793
Clone the repo, run iso dot s h, then qemu dot s h, and boot it.

